module Core

### Integer-indexed read access for ordered sequences (List, CircularList, Array, BitArray, BitList).
### Provides the `[]` subscript operator with U64 integer keys.
### Back-index (`^n`) is handled as a separate overload by each conforming type.
### Bounds violations throw at runtime.
### :typeparam V: The element type returned by the indexer.
protocol Indexable[AnyType V] obeys Sized
  ### Returns the element at zero-based position `index`.
  ### :param index: The zero-based position to read.
  ### :returns: The element at that position.
  ### :throws: {IndexOutOfBoundsError} if `index >= count()`.
  @readonly
  routine Me.getitem!(index: U64) -> V
